  "headBody": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<title>Letters from the edge | Example Notes</title>\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"Letters from the edge: a short essay used as a test page.\">\n<meta name=\"author\" content=\"Ines Varga\">\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"Letters from the edge\">\n<meta property=\"article:published_time\" content=\"2024-06-01T08:00:00Z\">\n</head>\n<body>\n<header><nav><a href=\"/\">Home</a> <a href=\"/about\">About</a></nav></header>\n<article>\n<h1>Letters from the edge</h1>\n<p class=\"byline\">By Ines Varga</p>\n<p>The committee met in the old library on the hill, where the winter light fell across the long oak tables, and the members argued, as they always did, about the cost of repairing the roof.</p>\n<p>Nobody could remember who had first proposed the plan, but by the second hour it had acquired the weight of tradition, and dissent, when it came, was polite and brief.</p>\n<p>In the end the treasurer produced a ledger, worn at the corners, and read out the figures in a flat voice that silenced the room, because the numbers, as ever, were worse than anyone had guessed.</p>\n<p>Outside, the river rose slowly against the stone bridge, carrying branches and the first ice of the year, and a boy on the far bank counted the pieces as they passed under the arch.</p><p>river harvest engine paper market garden signal winter lantern, letter bridge window river harvest engine paper market. garden, signal winter lantern letter bridge window river harvest engine, paper market garden<a id=\"footnote-anchor-1\" class=\"footnote-anchor\" href=\"#footnote-1\">1</a> and letter bridge window river harvest engine paper market garden, signal winter lantern.</p><p>winter lantern letter bridge window river harvest engine paper, market garden signal winter lantern letter bridge window. river, harvest engine paper market garden signal winter lantern letter, bridge window river<a id=\"footnote-anchor-2\" class=\"footnote-anchor\" href=\"#footnote-2\">2</a> and market garden signal winter lantern letter bridge window river, harvest engine paper.</p><p>engine paper market garden signal winter lantern letter bridge, window river harvest engine paper market garden signal. winter, lantern letter bridge window river harvest engine paper market, garden signal winter<a id=\"footnote-anchor-3\" class=\"footnote-anchor\" href=\"#footnote-3\">3</a> and window river harvest engine paper market garden signal winter, lantern letter bridge.</p><div class=\"footnote\" data-component-name=\"FootnoteToDOM\"><a id=\"footnote-1\" href=\"#footnote-anchor-1\" class=\"footnote-number\">1</a><div class=\"footnote-content\"><p>Note number 1 about river harvest engine paper market garden.</p></div></div><div class=\"footnote\" data-component-name=\"FootnoteToDOM\"><a id=\"footnote-2\" href=\"#footnote-anchor-2\" class=\"footnote-number\">2</a><div class=\"footnote-content\"><p>Note number 2 about winter lantern letter bridge window river.</p></div></div><div class=\"footnote\" data-component-name=\"FootnoteToDOM\"><a id=\"footnote-3\" href=\"#footnote-anchor-3\" class=\"footnote-number\">3</a><div class=\"footnote-content\"><p>Note number 3 about engine paper market garden signal winter.</p></div></div><p>In the end the treasurer produced a ledger, worn at the corners, and read out the figures in a flat voice that silenced the room, because the numbers, as ever, were worse than anyone had guessed.</p>\n<p>Outside, the river rose slowly against the stone bridge, carrying branches and the first ice of the year, and a boy on the far bank counted the pieces as they passed under the arch.</p>\n<p>The committee met in the old library on the hill, where the winter light fell across the long oak tables, and the members argued, as they always did, about the cost of repairing the roof.</p>\n<p>Nobody could remember who had first proposed the plan, but by the second hour it had acquired the weight of tradition, and dissent, when it came, was polite and brief.</p>\n</article>\n<footer><p>Copyright Example Notes</p></footer>\n</body>\n</html>\n"
